  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef Shahhoud wants to hire new chefs for his restaurant. Shahhoud posted a job offer on Chef Rami's paper \"Fast Food Times\".\n\nNNN candidates (numbered 111 through NNN) have applied for the job. There are MMM traits that define how good a chef is. You are given NNN strings S1,S2,…,SNS_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_NS1​,S2​,…,SN​ describing the traits of the candidates. Each of these strings has length MMM. For each valid iii and jjj, the jjj-th character of SiS_iSi​ is '1' if the iii-th chef has the jjj-th trait or '0' if this chef does not have this trait.\n\nShahhoud wants to choose a non-empty subsequence HHH (not necessarily contiguous) of the sequence (1,2,…,N)(1, 2, \\ldots, N)(1,2,…,N) and hire all candidates from HHH. However, the sequence HHH must satisfy an additional condition: for any two consecutive elements of HHH (let's denote them by xxx and yyy), candidates xxx and yyy have no common traits, to prevent fights between them.\n\nNow, Shahhoud is wondering: how many such valid subsequences exist? Find this number modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007 (109+710^9 + 7109+7).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤M≤161 \\le M \\le 161≤M≤16",
      "1≤N≤100,0001 \\le N \\le 100,0001≤N≤100,000",
      "∣Si∣=M|S_i| = M∣Si​∣=M for each valid iii",
      "S1,S2,…,SMS_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_MS1​,S2​,…,SM​ contain only characters '0' and '1'",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 500,000500,000500,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM.\nNNN lines follow. For each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), the iii-th of these lines contains a single string SiS_iSi​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the number of valid subsequences modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n4 2\n10\n01\n11\n10",
        "output": "7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: The valid subsequences are (1)(1)(1), (2)(2)(2), (3)(3)(3), (4)(4)(4), (1,2)(1,2)(1,2), (2,4)(2,4)(2,4) and (1,2,4)(1,2,4)(1,2,4)."
      }
    ]
  },
